

2024-04-02: An initial stab at 'more structured'
(by which I mean 'looks more like the relational model that I *really* want')
information about my prints, including different kinds of images.

I've been making OpenSCAD renderings by taking a screenshot,
then, in GIMP, cropping/scaling to 256x256, and converting
to indexed with 64 colors, then exporting as PNG, and saving under
//WSITEM-3326.1/share/2019/images/yayshots/2024/04/Plog46/STLRenderings/
(which isn't super important; it's just a scratch folder).

Note that `foo-file: <name> <uri>` and `foo-ref:
http://<resolver>/uri-res/raw/<uri>/<name>` can be considered
equivalent.


There are some different types of groups of parts.

A `part-set` is like a kit.  A specific set of parts that you might publish together.
As such, part set entries explicitly list the IDs of parts that comprise them,
like `members: ` + part IDs, comma-separated.

A `part-category` is a looser collection, more like a type.
Usually parts entries specify their categories as `member-of: ` + category IO.

The distinction is a fuzzy one.


