=part p1404
short-description: 2-inch x 4+1/2-inch x 1+1/2-inch experimental outlet holder
stl-file: p1404-OutletHolder0.1.stl	urn:bitprint:NVAWRWADKGDDXA4TGBAZWP6FZSN2KBRK.EIKQX3SJQ5VWGUCXVXZ6ICEZTJKN3ZOMLLWZVFI
openscad-rendering-ref: http://picture-files.nuke24.net/uri-res/raw/urn:bitprint:PD3H2UCWDF3ZYWDQMWZ4MZORQP7SYXC3.PH7QM4AHAWJEPYBVC34LH7WG2U6NR2DFCCYHNBA/p1404.png
photo-ref: http://picture-files.nuke24.net/uri-res/raw/urn:bitprint:EENJOWXVBAAHUE7XT6YPCCPK3WMQ3JPI.OYL2P3TBADQRTEQQZKNPJ3AM4O2U3FIX2A4JVRA/20250305_102710.jpg

An outlet holder in a TOGRack-ish enclosure.

Dimensions (width x height x depth):

- Upper cavity (fits front of outlet)   :: 1+3/4" x 4+1/4" x   1/4"
- Lower cavity (fits back of outlet)    :: 1+3/4" x 2+7/8" x 1+1/28"
- Outer dimensions                      :: 2"     x 4+1/2" x 1+1/2"
- Spacing between outlet mounting holes :: 3.281"

Finding: An unwired outlet fit snugly.
Would probably want more space for real use.
See WSITEM-201437's notes for more info.

