=narration 2026-05-31-some-wstypes

I put entries for WSTYPE-4143, WSTYPE-4144, and WSTYPE-4145 here
because they were referenced from some OpenSCAD parameter sets
but not, apparently, documented anywhere else, and though I have
so far avoided defining WSTYPEs in this file, this seems like
the most relevant place to put them.  So here you go.

=standard WSTYPE-4143
short-description: TOGridPile
doc-ref: https://www.nuke24.net/docs/2023/TOGridPile.html

=standard WSTYPE-4144
short-description: pegboard-mountable TOGridPile shelves, 26u

1/8" walls, making depth 1+1/2"xN + 1/4".  Grooves on sides 1/16"
deep, so that they fit into hooks with 26u (1+1/2"N + 1/8") space
between arms, e.g. p1519.  '26u' refers to the gap when N=1.

I later decided I prefer WSTYPE-4145, because it results in shelves
that are multiples of 1/2" deep, which means that they can themselves
be TOGridPile blocks.  '28u' refers to the gap when N=1.

=standard WSTYPE-4145
short-description: pegboard-mountable TOGridPile shelves, 28u

1/4" walls, making depth 1+1/2"xN + 1/2".  Grooves on sides 1/8"
deep, so that they fit into hooks with 28u (1+1/2"N + 1/4") space
between arms, e.g. p1757.

