=part p1853
short-description: first attempt at a holder for one of these 3/4-inch-wide razor blades
stl-file: p1853-RazorHolder1.0.stl	urn:bitprint:UZ5CU6YSN6YESNCTHZ2523BTFKE7VP7T.L5SVEY27AWZQDAH7N4PZEIJBWWHWHXOQBGWBH3A
openscad-rendering-ref: http://picture-files.nuke24.net/uri-res/raw/urn:bitprint:E4KWNFLY44YU6VRZGTKNOXNA5T2SPG5R.P75CJP2ID5Y7BMA4E2WU5JV46AQ3WGOG3FP2E2Q/p1853.png

Goal is to have a way of holding one at the end of a bar to scrape circular holes in plastic or something.

For this version, I have a pocket in one side that's just barely deep enough
to hold the razor blade.  Ideally less deep, so that when it's clamped together
against another surface, the blade is held firmly in place.

In practice, I found the pocket isn't really deep enough to catch the edge of the blade.
A better design might have an arbitrearily deep pocket (1/8", let's say)
and a matching anti-pocket on the mating piece to fill the pocket and
hold the blade in place.

