=part p1859
short-description: 1/4-inch thick bar of #6-32-UNC-threaded test holes
stl-file: p1859.stl	urn:bitprint:SEKWK5ROZ2EUXCODM5DOK64LJLXBU5HR.MLU4TVIXZQ42CGXYPZUACNO7PGO43YAAJMMDCOI
openscad-rendering-ref: http://picture-files.nuke24.net/uri-res/raw/urn:bitprint:LNUB4HLP7KM7RV4JEQPT5CVQKCZFJRJQ.CAC6JKD45FKN7NHTP7N5XKCOHLW3AGDPN3VGTWA/p1859.png
openscad-rendering-ref: http://picture-files.nuke24.net/uri-res/raw/urn:bitprint:GPJEXWDS67QDNIFPYDHV2VHDPN6CIWGO.KVULE3DGPHFR4W4DDM6M6IZFVLEL5YYXKGS4K3A/p1859b.png
photo-ref: http://picture-files.nuke24.net/uri-res/raw/urn:bitprint:W3QPW5ZGEOYCI4NOFD4SRL3EPA4TXSJ2.4QY7KHK23ANSBB6DEYI4ZHIODR57AWEY66ZEQAQ/20250322_180510.jpg

Findings, after printing 2025-03-22T15:23-E3 (p1859e, 1.0035 scale,
0.2mm layers, 0.4mm nozzle, WSITEM-201491 and WSITEM-201492):

- 0.30mm :: Can thread in with fingers
- 0.20mm :: Can thread in relatively easily with screwdriver
- 0.10mm :: Can thread in with screwdriver, but sticky
- 0.05mm :: Can thread in with screwdriver, just barely
- 0.00mm :: Cannot get the screw started

So, anywhere from 0.05mm to 0.3mm works.  Maybe 0.2mm is a good middle-of-the-road default.


=part p1860
short-description: 1/4-inch thick bar of 1/4-20-UNC-threaded test holes
stl-file: p1860-ThreadTest2.stl	urn:bitprint:MYHHAUC3W2K6EMFQYQQGLA2Z2KSQPEKW.VEPMZ4IV73HY7UNJP2DJHZDEDRFQE2I2JZXCHTY
openscad-rendering-ref: http://picture-files.nuke24.net/uri-res/raw/urn:bitprint:PDQZY675KYCUKI3NNVFIZ3KI4Y4P5VP7.3O3MN32V7B6OTTRBRPZCDP6RLHFHYKSVJLO36OI/p1860.png

Findings, after printing 2025-03-22T18:18-E3 (p1860e, 1.0035 scale,
0.2mm layers, 0.4mm nozzle, WSITEM-201480 and WSITEM-201490):

- 0.00mm :: Can thread in with some force; wrench required to get it through the back, deforming the plastic in back
- 0.05mm :: Can thread in with some force; wrench required to get it through the back, deforming the plastic in back
- 0.10mm :: Can thread through with fingers; wrench required to get it through the back
- 0.15mm :: Can thread through with fingers, though it is a little tight
- 0.20mm :: Can thread through with fingers, though it is a little tight
- 0.25mm :: Can thread in easily with fingers; gets tight through the back; bolt wiggles a little
- 0.30mm :: Can thread in easily with fingers, all the way through; bolt wiggles a little

Like with the #6s, 0.20mm might be a safe default.

