=part p2051
short-description: 1/4-inch-thick threaded holes for #6-32s demo
stl-file: p2051.stl	urn:bitprint:DXMQ3XXGGSSRURR4NYB2KWP2D56G3RYM.L6S4PBQBZKAT5YJZTUW767MHQZZUQSWC4FSMKEQ
openscad-rendering-ref: http://picture-files.nuke24.net/uri-res/raw/urn:bitprint:MBLVYQNAXLTPPJK6TULBYFTLT34MDHYE.HD23PSJJXVEKEV7EQCI6TJL7GAZ7BV6BAJ7QIHI/p2051.png

Demonstration of a 1/4" wide wall that #6-32s can thread into, to see if I can, by printing the threads (sideways).

In practice (when printed on my Kobra Max with 0.8mm nozzle), the holes are fiddly and the labels are a mess.
So maybe just use square holes, a la p2052.

=part p2052
short-description: 1/4-inch-thick square holes for #6-32s demo
stl-file: p2052.stl	urn:bitprint:MPDXOYHZXV7V34DO4ASLJZBZXD7HCGSJ.VJW2TMNYW5K2Q5FXOCYDTIV7V4X36IKZJXGJ64I
