Demonstration of a 1/4" wide wall that #6-32s can thread into, to see if I can,
by printing square holes that the threads will crush their way into.

Works okay.  Easier to thread into than p2051's threaded holes, and definitely a simpler polyhedron.

=part p2053
short-description: 1+1/2-inch x 1+1/2-inch x 2-inch TOGridPile cup with Clarp2505-compatible sublip
stl-file: p2053.stl	urn:bitprint:5WKQFPXT2WQSMUSCQE5E2AHEGNEFIAYC.UA5YPGL6QDP2PQ4J5JDEK7FC36XDVVG5IKXLLHY
openscad-rendering-ref: http://picture-files.nuke24.net/uri-res/raw/urn:bitprint:PW2X5MII7G5X24X5RPGF37WOHPZHDAXL.TBUECNXTYSHMTKJPMHMWOAXJK3ZVILMUXFDG2OI/p2053.png

It bothered me that the TGx11.1 cups' sublips were almost, but not quite,
compatible with Clarp2505-M clips, so I adjusted the design slightly
and made this as a prototype.

Clip (probably p1991-based) clips in great.

This might not be the ideal sublip shape, but I think it's fine as the default
shape for the 'prototype TGx11.1-based cup' design, which is what TGx11.1.scad is.

