=part-category p2360
short-description: 2-inch desiccant holder system

Primary connection: 2-4+1/2-UNC threads.

Sections have up to 2+1/8" outer diameter, since that is about the
largest diameter that can fit through the smallest of the 'axle holes'
of the 3D printer spools that I have (some are much larger).

Circular couplers are also 2+1/8".  Octagonal or other shapes can be larger.

1+3/4-inch diameter discs can serve as bulkheads between sections,
since they fit inside a 2"-4+1/2 threaded hole, with 1/12" or 2mm
being a common thickness.

=part-category p2369
short-description: simple 1+1/2-inch square spacers

Probably generated by Spacer.scad.

=part-category p2370
short-description: BrickHolder2-based parts

Outer sizes are multiples of 1/2".

Inner dimensions are nominally multiples of 1/2", also, such that walls are 1/4" thick.

Some models have larger 'inner margins' (up to 3mm) to accomodate bricks that are just slighly larger,
such as p1648, which holds, as I recall, Dellie's power brick.

As an alternative to rectangular inner margin,
some models have an additional cylindrical 'can cutout'
in order that they can hold e.g. pop cans that would otherwise
not quite fit.  e.g. p1572 can hold a 68mm-diameter can.

Sides are often (but not always) 'hatom-segmented'.

=part-category p2371
short-description: open-sided/bottomed BrickHolder2-based parts

Slot in front and hole in bottom allow power bricks to be slid in
without unplugging them.

Used for holding power bricks, single cans/jars, or spray bottles.

TODO: Identify more parts that belong to this category

=part-category p2372
short-description: 'dunkers'; usually closed-sided BrickHolder2s

Water-tight on 5 sides, open on the top.

Used for holding gridbeam (or similar) as it soaks up oil.

TODO: Identify more parts that belong to this category

=part-category p2378
short-description: 'dunker caps'; usually short, closed-sided BrickHolder2s

These are essentially the same design as p2372s,
except that they tend to be relatively short (1 inch or so),
have small inner margins (0.1mm), and are 1/2" wider than
the dunkers that they cap.

=part-category p2373
short-description: box-like BrickHolder2s

Similar to dunkers, but may have screw holes in bottom and/or sides.

Commonly used as wall boxes.

TODO: Identify more parts that belong to this category

