Findings (via p23922 / 2026-01-26T17:21-E3 / WSITEM-202092):
- Not exactly tight, but kind of a trick to get it into the ThinkPad dock holder
- Holds the PoE switch, but just barely.

Potential improvements:
- Fix the width, obviously (p2393 does this, probably)
- Slightly bevel bottom corners so that they don't need to be sanded
- Taller
- Wider front slot (can be almost the width of the switch)
- A 'standardizing' (i.e. interior is the next smaller 1/2" size) adapter might not be a terrible idea!

