=part p2503
short-description: 2x1x2-chunk JetKVM holder
obsoleted-by: p2504
stl-file: p2503.stl	urn:bitprint:ZRPZS7HLJFAIU3VNTBXAMUCSIPKUIQXB.NBXXOBRDWUEFC33W2YNONZHXAQHWYJYZ4UMVBBQ
openscad-rendering-ref: http://picture-files.nuke24.net/uri-res/raw/urn:bitprint:4TNQZEZT7MZC62MDEOUZQJ2KR2AA46C6.6RTU7FHGMVEZHRQZP5J5FDKWYRCWFVURRLPLOTY/p2503.png

Works fine.  That said:

- Could benefit from a slot in the front so that the JetKVM
  can be inserted/removed without having to unplug the cords.
- Could hold the JetKVM slightly lower to make room for a small
  lip at the top, to hold the JetKVM more securely when the
  whole thing is set on its back.
- Could hold the JetKVM slightly farther back
  (maybe 3/16" from the back instead of 1/4")
  so that the top of the JetKVM doesn't protrude from the front.

=part p2504
short-description: 2x1x2-chunk JetKVM holder
obsoleted-by: p2505
stl-file: p2504.stl	urn:bitprint:ZUAK2IPGYCPO64MAW7XDFJ4RKDX2CJZC.FRJ74EEEU2SBPJJFXZI6DKXJWH557HZI6Z3BIQQ
