=part p2552
short-description: Dad's 'Expensive_RoundThermometerMount'
stl-file: p2552-Expensive_RoundThermometerMount.stl	urn:bitprint:7NVPYF4HVQHP3ISTC7ON5IS6X2MOBDJZ.2MLZ7THSKIEPAPN5Q5LC2CLKZ6DWEMUJ4ASY3YA
openscad-rendering-ref: http://picture-files.nuke24.net/uri-res/raw/urn:bitprint:V5VZGXZXMMVIXIHLHQQGDYIVHRXFTMNM.YREI35QLVHMUZOQSS75MAR6SE6WWGRPC3IM3FLY/p2552-Expensive_RoundThermometerMount.png

I suspect that this has an approximate 1.0035 scale built-in,
because Dad doesn't like to scale when he prints.
p2552a8z / 2026-05-21T14:55-KM is to test this.

The print failed due to not enough material stuck to the plate,
but it was enough to find that this does *not* require
additional scaling-up.

In other words, the p2552 STL has a baked-in 1.0035 (or so) scale,
and the actual object should be about 0.9965 as big.

