- Button slides in very nicely, and the nut turns easily

=part p2554
short-description: 4-chunk x 1-chunk x 3/4-inch ButtonBlock0.2
tags: ButtonBlock0
stl-file: p2554.stl	urn:bitprint:QUONROOVTGA6C7KDGOKAGIMBWO5L3HSP.XQWAA2KL3LDHTKZMXSO3GUM6EVDX2L2COOBREAA
openscad-rendering-ref: http://picture-files.nuke24.net/uri-res/raw/urn:bitprint:4DEDJHR4DAILK7RGZD4C4S5IEICX4JJ7.TMKPN2AGAHGPOLJE4V5ECLIYCNEVWC66GCQNIEQ/p2554.png

With holes for 2.1mm barrel inlets in chunk center fronts.

Finding (via p2554a8a / 2026-05-23T00:37-KM / WSITEM-202320):
- Barrel connectors are a bit snug
- Impossible to get nuts onto barrel jacks after they're inserted all the way
- Won't be able to use the screw holes in the back and the barrel jacks
  at the same time because the leads on the end of the jack sit
  almost directly over where the screw osuld go through.
  It might work if the leads were bent, but I don't want to do that.
- Won't be able to use the wire slots on the back side
  if the back of the block butts up against another gridbeam.
  This could be fixed by making the wire slot also include
  a notch in the bottom.

=part p2555
short-description: 5-chunk x 1-chunk x 3/4-inch ButtonBlock0.2
tags: ButtonBlock0
stl-file: p2555.stl	urn:bitprint:QFCZT4CCYX7SON7PQ5RAH3D653QRYSJ7.ZKGHAMWJVGW2R2Z23X7YNZDJAC6DCKRQIELIMHA
openscad-rendering-ref: http://picture-files.nuke24.net/uri-res/raw/urn:bitprint:OCGUCZB26BSR6MO26VF2ZNM3AUX2BABE.GW75LI7YFEJDBJQFURQCXLAAE2TAC3E6W7PYJYA/p2555.png

With holes for 2.1mm barrel inlets in chunk center fronts.

Same as p2554, just 5 chunks instead of 4.
See notes on p2554 for findings/thoughts.

=part p2556
short-description: 5-chunk x 1-chunk x 3/4-inch ButtonBlock0.3 with barrel jacks in front and wire-slot-2s in back
tags: ButtonBlock0
stl-file: p2556.stl	urn:bitprint:HGE5JRHRJUHNCEWEG2UZ4I4NKDU2GKYK.TKPQNLGICCE7B7JB73JNUX7MW36KOU2Z5ZR2L7A
openscad-rendering-ref: http://picture-files.nuke24.net/uri-res/raw/urn:bitprint:M75E7T2GP7SEHCCDYL2EPJVLU4GI7AWD.42WVSZCNYGTVFUZCU64L6NDWGZ6VWWRNIFLUEPQ/p2556.png

This design attempts to address the 'useless wire slots' problem of
p2554 and p2555 by having the wire slots go all the way through the bottom.

This is all well and good,
but still has the problem that you can't use
both the screw holes and the barrel jacks at the same time.

And if you want to use the wire slots,
they're on the opposite side from the buttons,
and going through the bottom won't help if the thing
is pressed up against some gridbeam.

It might be easuer to just use the barrel jacks.

